entity.css"><link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/assets/images/portfolio-icon-180.png"><link rel="manifest" href="/site.webmanifest"></head><body data-page="resources.html" class="academy page-library master-refresh reference-page"><header class="academy-header" id="top"><a class="academy-brand personal-brand" href="/"><span>Bakhtawar Khan<small>Personal Digital Portfolio · MBK Global</small></span></a><button class="academy-menu" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="academy-nav">Menu <span>+</span></button><nav id="academy-nav" aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="/">Home</a><a href='/about'>About</a><a href='/projects'>Projects</a><a href='/services'>Services</a><a class='header-cta' href='/hire-me'>Let’s talk <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><details class="portfolio-more"><summary>More</summary><div class="portfolio-panel"><section><h2>Professional work</h2><a href='/case-studies'>Case Studies</a><a href='/changelog'>Projects Changelog</a><a href='/delivered-project'>Process</a><a href='/resources'>Resources</a><a href='/news'>Notes</a></section><section><h2>Contact &amp; career</h2><a href='/book-a-call'>Book a Call</a><a href='/resume'>Resume / CV</a><a href='/hire-me'>Hire Me</a></section><section><h2>Content &amp; media</h2><a href='/gallery'>Gallery</a><a href='/blog'>Blog &amp; Articles</a><a href='/faq'>FAQs</a></section><section><h2>Personal brand</h2><a href='/about-muhammad-bakhtawar-khan'>Founder Profile</a><a href='/social'>Social Profiles</a><a href='/official-links'>Official Links</a></section></div></details><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" aria-label="Switch color theme">◐</button></nav></header>
<a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a><main class="wrap inner-page academy-main" id="main-content"><section class="academy-page-hero"><div class="academy-breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href='/resources'>Explore MBK</a></div><div class="academy-kicker">library <span> / MBK GLOBAL</span></div><h1 class="page-title">Useful starting points, <em>not noise.</em></h1><p class="page-intro">A growing library of practical references for building and maintaining digital projects. Start with official documentation, test changes carefully and document what you learn.</p></section><section class="editorial-section"><div class="editorial-label">01 / WORKING REFERENCES</div><div><h2>Find the right reference, then test it.</h2><p>A curated starting point—not a list of endorsements or affiliations. External documentation can move or require an account. Check the current provider terms before implementing; these links have not been live-verified in this session.</p><label for="resource-filter">Find a resource by topic, tool or purpose</label><input type="search" id="resource-filter" placeholder="Try Telegram, security, React…"><p id="resource-count" aria-live="polite"></p><div class="resource-index"><article data-resource><span class="academy-kicker">Developer tools</span><h3><a href="https://developer.chrome.com/docs/devtools/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Chrome DevTools ↗</a></h3><small>Official documentation</small><p>Inspect layout, network requests and performance before guessing at a fix.</p></article><article data-resource><span class="academy-kicker">JavaScript &amp; React</span><h3><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">MDN JavaScript ↗</a></h3><small>Documentation reference</small><p>Understand language behavior, modules, asynchronous code and browser APIs.</p></article><article data-resource><span class="academy-kicker">JavaScript &amp; React</span><h3><a href="https://react.dev/learn" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">React Learn ↗</a></h3><small>Official documentation</small><p>Learn components, state and data flow; build small interfaces before adding libraries.</p></article><article data-resource><span class="academy-kicker">Web &amp; application development</span><h3><a href="https://developer.android.com/develop" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Android Developers ↗</a></h3><small>Official documentation</small><p>Explore Android architecture and platform fundamentals; this is a learning resource, not a claim of shipped Android work.</p></article><article data-resource><span class="academy-kicker">AI &amp; chatbot development</span><h3><a href="https://platform.openai.com/docs/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OpenAI API documentation ↗</a></h3><small>Official documentation</small><p>Review model APIs, tool calling and usage constraints; paid access and privacy review may be required.</p></article><article data-resource><span class="academy-kicker">APIs &amp; integrations</span><h3><a href="https://learning.postman.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Postman Learning Center ↗</a></h3><small>Official tool documentation</small><p>Create repeatable request tests and inspect response schemas without exposing private tokens.</p></article><article data-resource><span class="academy-kicker">WhatsApp &amp; Telegram bots</span><h3><a href="https://developers.facebook.com/docs/whatsapp/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WhatsApp Business Platform ↗</a></h3><small>Official documentation</small><p>Check business access, supported messages, pricing and current platform requirements.</p></article><article data-resource><span class="academy-kicker">WhatsApp &amp; Telegram bots</span><h3><a href="https://core.telegram.org/bots/api" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Telegram Bot API ↗</a></h3><small>Official documentation</small><p>Review bot commands, webhook methods, updates and platform limits.</p></article><article data-resource><span class="academy-kicker">Security &amp; code analysis</span><h3><a href="https://owasp.org/www-project-web-security-testing-guide/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OWASP Web Security Testing Guide ↗</a></h3><small>Community reference</small><p>Plan authorized testing with explicit scope; never use it as permission to test another system.</p></article><article data-resource><span class="academy-kicker">Security &amp; code analysis</span><h3><a href="https://ghidra-sre.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ghidra ↗</a></h3><small>Open-source tool</small><p>Explore code analysis on software you own or have permission to inspect; consider legal and licence constraints.</p></article><article data-resource><span class="academy-kicker">SEO, AEO &amp; GEO</span><h3><a href="https://developers.google.com/search/docs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Search Central ↗</a></h3><small>Official documentation</small><p>Check crawling, metadata and structured-data eligibility; no tool guarantees rankings or AI citations.</p></article><article data-resource><span class="academy-kicker">Automation &amp; workflows</span><h3><a href="https://docs.n8n.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">n8n documentation ↗</a></h3><small>Official tool documentation</small><p>Map triggers, credentials, retries and failure paths before enabling an automation.</p></article><article data-resource><span class="academy-kicker">Design &amp; accessibility</span><h3><a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/tutorials/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WAI Tutorials ↗</a></h3><small>Standards guidance</small><p>Design forms, navigation and images with accessibility built into the implementation.</p></article><article data-resource><span class="academy-kicker">Deployment &amp; cloud</span><h3><a href="https://vercel.com/docs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Vercel documentation ↗</a></h3><small>Official documentation</small><p>Review deployment environments, domains and runtime boundaries.</p></article><article data-resource><span class="academy-kicker">Productivity &amp; open source</span><h3><a href="https://docs.github.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Docs ↗</a></h3><small>Official documentation</small><p>Organize issues, document changes and review source code before reusing a dependency.</p></article></div></div></section><p class="eyebrow">RESOURCE LIBRARY / PRACTICAL NOTES</p>
<div class="service-grid"><article class="service-item"><span class="service-number">01 / WEB FOUNDATIONS</span><h2 id="section-1">HTML, CSS &amp; JavaScript</h2><p>Use semantic HTML, responsive layouts, accessible controls and clear JavaScript states. Build a small feature, test it on mobile and add useful error messages before adding complexity.</p><p><a class="article-link" href="https://developer.mozilla.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">MDN Web Docs ↗</a></p></article><article class="service-item"><span class="service-number">02 / REACT</span><h2 id="section-2">Component thinking</h2><p>Split interfaces into reusable components, keep data flow understandable, and make loading, empty, error and success states intentional.</p><p><a class="article-link" href="https://react.dev/learn" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">React Learn ↗</a></p></article><article class="service-item"><span class="service-number">03 / API WORK</span><h2 id="section-3">Integration checklist</h2><p>Check authentication, rate limits, error responses, CORS, timeouts, data validation and secret handling. Never expose private API keys in client-side code.</p><p><a class="article-link" href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">HTTP documentation ↗</a></p></article><article class="service-item"><span class="service-number">04 / SEARCH</span><h2 id="section-4">Technical SEO basics</h2><p>Give each page a unique title and description, use descriptive headings and links, create a valid sitemap, check canonical URLs and make sure important content is crawlable.</p><p><a class="article-link" href="https://developers.google.com/search/docs/fundamentals/seo-starter-guide" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Google SEO Starter Guide ↗</a></p></article><article class="service-item"><span class="service-number">05 / QUALITY</span><h2 id="section-5">Performance &amp; accessibility</h2><p>Compress images, avoid unnecessary scripts, use keyboard-friendly controls, maintain contrast and test real phone widths. Measure before and after performance changes.</p><p><a class="article-link" href="https://web.dev/articles/vitals" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Web Vitals ↗</a> · <a class="article-link" href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/quickref/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">WCAG 2.2 ↗</a></p></article><article class="service-item"><span class="service-number">06 / AI &amp; AUTOMATION</span><h2 id="section-6">Start with a clear workflow</h2><p>Define the input, output, failure cases and human review step. Use sample data first and avoid giving automations more access than they need.</p><p><a class='article-link' href='/blog'>Read MBK articles ↗</a></p></article></div>
<section aria-label="MBK SEO and technology guides" class="identity-grid"><article class="identity-card"><p class="eyebrow">SEO · AEO · GEO</p><h2 id="section-7">Search visibility guides by Bakhtawar Khan (MBK)</h2><p>Practical notes on technical SEO, answer-ready content and entity clarity for the MBK personal portfolio and MBK Global.</p><ul><li><a href='/muhammad-bakhtawar-khan-digital-portfolio'>Bakhtawar Khan (MBK): A Digital Portfolio Built Around Practical Projects</a></li><li><a href='/seo-aeo-geo-for-personal-brands'>SEO, AEO and GEO for a Personal Brand: The MBK Approach</a></li><li><a href='/technical-seo-checklist-mbk'>Technical SEO Checklist for a Portfolio Website</a></li><li><a href='/answer-engine-content-design'>Designing Answer-Ready Content for AEO</a></li><li><a href='/generative-search-entity-clarity'>Entity Clarity for Generative Search: Person, Brand and Projects</a></li><li><a href='/article-api-integration'>API Integration for Modern Web Projects</a></li><li><a href='/web-security-basics-for-small-sites'>Web Security Basics for Small Websites</a></li></ul></article><article class="identity-card"><h2 id="section-8">Official MBK destinations</h2><p>Start from verified first-party destinations rather than copied profile data.</p><p><a href='/about-muhammad-bakhtawar-khan'>Bakhtawar Khan — Founder Profile</a></p><p><a href='/official-links'>MBK Official Links &amp; Projects</a></p><p><a href='/social'>MBK Social Profiles</a></p><p><a href="https://mr-bakhtawar.netlify.app/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">MBK Global website ↗</a></p></article></section><section class="service-intro"><h2 id="section-9">How this library will be maintained.</h2><div><p>Resources should be checked for accuracy and updated when tools or documentation change. These links are starting points, not a substitute for testing a real implementation.</p><p><a class='button button-primary' href='/contact'>Ask about a project ↗</a></p></div></section><details class="academy-directory"><summary>Explore the complete MBK directory <span>+</span></summary><section aria-labelledby="mbk-directory-heading" class="section wrap mbk-site-directory"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">MBK PORTFOLIO / SITE DIRECTORY</p><h2 id="mbk-directory-heading">Explore the <em>full portfolio.</em></h2></div><p class="page-intro">Browse Bakhtawar Khan (MBK), MBK Global projects, services, technical guides and official contact resources.</p></div><div class="mbk-directory-group"><h3>Profile &amp; contact</h3><ul><li><a href='/about-muhammad-bakhtawar-khan'>Mr. Bakhtawar | Founder of MBK Global <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></li><li><a href='/about'>About Bakhtawar Khan (MBK) <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></li><li><a href='/book-a-call'>Book a Call | Bakhtawar Khan <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></li><li><a href='/case-studies'>Digital Project Case Studies | Bakhtawar Khan (MBK) <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></li><li><a href='/changelog'>Website Changelog <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></li><li><a href='/contact'>Contact Bakhtawar Khan (MBK) <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></li><li><a href='/delivered-project'>Project Process &amp; Delivery | Bakhtawar Khan (MBK) <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></li><li><a href='/faq'>FAQs | Bakhtawar Khan (MBK) Digital Services <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></li><li><a href='/gallery'>Bakhtawar Khan Photos &amp; Portfolio Gallery | MBK <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></li><li><a href='/hire-me'>Hire Bakhtawar Khan (MBK) | Web, API &amp; Automation <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></li><li><a href="/">Mr. Bakhtawar | Founder of MBK Global — Web Development, AI &amp; Digital Technology <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></li><li><a href='/muhammad-bakhtawar-khan-digital-portfolio'>Bakhtawar Khan (MBK): A Digital Portfolio Built Around Practical Projects <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></li><li><a href='/official-links'>Official Links &amp; P